ErrorDIASCodeMustBe5Digits=The DIAS merchant code must be five digits starting with 9
DIASCodeUsage=DIAS code usage
DIASCodeUsageHelp=Digit 10 of a DIAS reference, after RF, the two check digits and your DIAS code. It tells the paying bank how to check the payment and must match the setup your bank registered with DIAS. If unsure, ask your bank.
DIASCodeUsage8=8 - Same code for credit transfer and direct debit
DIASCodeUsage9=9 - Separate codes for credit transfer and direct debit
ErrorDIASReferenceAmountChecked=This DIAS reference has 0 to 7 at digit 10, so the bank checks it against one fixed amount and would reject other amounts. It cannot be used for several invoices. Ask your bank for a reference with 8 or 9 at digit 10.
WarningPaymentRefDIASCodeMissing=No payment reference can be generated until the DIAS merchant code is set in Home - Setup - Company. Invoices validated before then will carry no reference.
WarningPaymentRefDIASCodeMissingThirdparty=References already written on a third party will keep being used. A third party that has none yet gets no reference until the DIAS merchant code is set in Home - Setup - Company.
WarningPaymentRefPaymentIdMissing=No payment identifier is set in Home - Setup - Company, so every invoice would share the same default reference.
